nding through each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" in order to an unvisited vertex (Mathematica ","type":"text"},{"code":"FindHamiltonianPath","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":").","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Self-loops never help; one vertex is the trivial path. Pruning cuts only subtrees with no","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"solution (an unvisited vertex unreachable, or left without a usable predecessor or","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"successor), so it keeps the order. Without a start the search is run again from each","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex in turn until one succeeds, so a graph with no Hamiltonian path costs n searches.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://Tours/documentation/Tours/GraphProtocols/DirectedGraph/shortestTour(weight:)":{"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/tours\/graphprotocols\/directedgraph\/shortesttour(weight:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/Tours\/documentation\/Tours\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph\/shortestTour(weight:)","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shortestTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Cycle","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:5Walks5CycleV"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Vertex","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Edges","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P5EdgesQa"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Index","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"text":">?","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"shortestTour(weight:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest directed tour (the asymmetric travelling salesman problem), by the same"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Held–Karp program as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph.shortestTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeldKarpTSP"},{"type":"text","text":" on a directed"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"graph): the least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple digraph, each step along an arc"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from one vertex to the next, or nil when there is none; among the optimal ones, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first vertex. Self-loops are"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored and each ordered pair is joined by its lightest arc (the earliest position on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ties), which is the edge the returned "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Cycle"},{"type":"text","text":" uses, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"cycle.weight(weight)"},{"type":"text","text":" is the tour’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"length. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" is called once per non-loop edge, in position order. nil below three"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"vertices, as on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" (an antiparallel pair is a "},{"type":"c